{
  "id": "adjektive-nach-sein",
  "name": "Adjectives: agreement and position",
  "level": "A1",
  "status": "entwurf",
  "variety": "es-ES",
  "source": "icanspeak Spanish original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-04)",
  "subtitle": "An adjective matches its noun in gender and number, and it usually comes after the noun: una casa blanca, los coches nuevos.",
  "briefMarks": ["-o", "-a", "-os", "-as"],
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "article", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "noun" },
      { "text": "adjective", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "<span class=\"vp-prep\">un</span> piso <span class=\"vp-verb\">pequeño</span> · <span class=\"vp-prep\">una</span> casa <span class=\"vp-verb\">pequeña</span> · <span class=\"vp-prep\">los</span> pisos <span class=\"vp-verb\">pequeños</span> · <span class=\"vp-prep\">las</span> casas <span class=\"vp-verb\">pequeñas</span>",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "Adjectives in <strong>-o</strong> have four forms: <em>alto, alta, altos, altas</em>. <em>Mi hermano es alto. Mi hermana es alta.</em>",
        "tag": "Four forms"
      },
      {
        "html": "Adjectives in <strong>-e</strong> or a consonant have one form for both genders, and a plural: <em>un piso grande, una casa grande, unos pisos grandes</em>; <em>un libro fácil, unas clases fáciles</em>.",
        "tag": "Two forms"
      },
      {
        "html": "Nationalities in a consonant add <strong>-a</strong> for women: <em>español → española, inglés → inglesa, alemán → alemana</em>. The accent goes away.",
        "tag": "Nationalities"
      },
      {
        "html": "The adjective usually comes <strong>after</strong> the noun: <em>un coche rojo, una mujer simpática</em>. Not: <em>un rojo coche</em>.",
        "tag": "Position"
      },
      {
        "html": "After <em>ser</em> and <em>estar</em>, the adjective still matches the subject: <em>La calle es tranquila. Los niños están cansados.</em>",
        "tag": "After ser and estar"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>la casa blanco</em> → ✓ <em>la casa blanca</em>. ✗ <em>los pisos caro</em> → ✓ <em>los pisos caros</em>. ✗ <em>un rojo coche</em> → ✓ <em>un coche rojo</em>. Some adjectives can come first, like <em>buen</em> and <em>gran</em>. You will see them at B1. Revise <a href=\"/plurals\">Plurals</a>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
